## 4. Curried API & DX Specification

### Left-to-Right Curried Drawing Model

Curried signatures strictly follow the **Style $\rightarrow$ Geometry $\rightarrow$ Target/Context $\rightarrow$ Driver** order:

```typescript
// Signature: drawCircle(color)(radius)(position)(driver)
drawCircle('#ff0055')(25)({ x: 100, y: 150 })(driver);

// Signature: drawRect(color)(dimensions)(position)(driver)
drawRect('rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1)')({ w: 40, h: 40 })({ x: 0, y: 0 })(driver);

```

### Partial Application & Composition Advantage

Because the API is curried, partial application allows building domain-specific mini-libraries effortlessly:

```typescript
// Pre-configure style & radius once outside the loop
const drawRedNode = drawCircle('rgb(220, 50, 50)')(12);
const drawGoldNode = drawCircle('#ffd700')(8);

// Inside the render loop: execute with remaining arguments (position & driver)
export const renderGraph = (driver, nodes) => {
  nodes.forEach((node) => {
    const drawFn = node.isImportant ? drawGoldNode : drawRedNode;
    drawFn(node.position)(driver);
  });
};

```

